# Pairs with ClaimHeadCoversPriorAppends. The claim returns the readable head -
# the end of the durable contiguous prefix - instead of the allocator head. An
# append allocated but not yet durable sits above it, so it is not below the
# head the raised activation replays to. The module does not model durability,
# so the readable head is any offset at or below the allocator head. Moved from
# the design's ReadPositionHonestClaimReadableHead.
MODULE: ClaimHeadCoversPriorAppendsClaimReadableHead
TARGET: ClaimHeadCoversPriorAppends
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the claim returns the shard's readable head, not its allocator's next offset
PERTURBS: ClaimRaise

--- FIND
    /\ claimHead' = [claimHead EXCEPT ![a] = next]
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the readable head, which lags the allocator head by any append in flight.
    /\ \E h \in 0..next : claimHead' = [claimHead EXCEPT ![a] = h]
--- END
